-- erwartet: N380
-- **An `atomic` array whose length is not a compile-time constant: nothing
-- says what "in range" means, so no access to it has a bound.**
--
-- `M103` compares the index range against the LENGTH, and a length that did
-- not fold leaves it with no number to compare against -- the rule does not
-- even match its own arm (`Typ::Feld { laenge: None }`) and stays silent.
-- Measured 2026-09-16 through the unchanged checker: this file, with the index
-- reaching 300 over a `static` length of 256, reported `0 errors, 0 hints`.
--
-- On an ordinary table that silence is old and shared. Here it is one step
-- worse, and that step is why `N380` exists: an `atomic` carrier is the ONE
-- carrier the goal theorem exempts from race freedom (`RennfreiBis`,
-- `Zielsatz/Akzeptiert.lean` `atomarB`), so an out-of-range atomic
-- read-modify-write is an unchecked write to an arbitrary address that nothing
-- else in the statement covers -- not the footprint, not the guard, not race
-- freedom.
--
-- The emitter has its own half of this: it refuses the DECLARATION too
-- (`C001`, *"`atomic` array whose length is not a compile-time constant"*),
-- because `[]` at file scope is an incomplete type and a guessed size is a
-- buffer nobody asked for.
module gift::atomic_array_length_not_constant {

static WIE_VIELE : u32 = 256;

atomic REGEL : [u32; WIE_VIELE] relaxed;

impl fn setz(r : u32 in 0 .. 300, v : u32)
    effects { writes REGEL }
    costs   <= 4 ops
{
    REGEL[r] = v publishes nothing;
}

}
